{{also|Neurotransmitter}}
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|neuro-|transmitter}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|biochemistry|neuroscience}} Any [[substance]], such as [[acetylcholine]] or [[dopamine]], responsible for sending [[nerve]] [[signal]]s across a [[synapse]] between two [[neuron]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=David R. Hawkins|title=The Eye of the I: From Which Nothing is Hidden|page=142
|passage=Together with this is the influence of an infinite number of '''neurotransmitters''', neurohormones, environmental hazards, and accidental programmings.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Kristen Rogers|title=If antidepressants are killing your sex life, here’s what you can do|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/03/21/health/antidepressants-sexual-side-effects-tips-wellness/index.html|date=2024-03-21|passage=The class of antidepressants most commonly associated with sexual dysfunction is selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, or SSRIs, which treat depression by ultimately increasing levels of the '''neurotransmitter''' serotonin in the brain.}}

